# What a repo needs to run this action. These are GitHub Actions SECRETS, not a
# file you commit: this file only documents the names.
#
#   gh secret set AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY --repo OWNER/REPO
#
# The same names work for running scripts/ locally (see AGENTS.md, "Testing a
# change"): copy to .env, fill in, `set -a; source .env; set +a`. .env is
# gitignored.

# Required. A Vercel AI Gateway key with its own budget; the gateway enforces
# the cap and returns a 402. Make a dedicated one, not the key you code with:
#   vercel ai-gateway api-keys create --name github-actions --budget 10 --refresh-period monthly
AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# Optional, only for a bot with its own name and for CI to run on the PRs it
# opens (README, "A bot with its own name"). A GitHub App you own.
# FX_APP_ID=
# FX_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Local testing only. The workflow token replaces this on a runner.
# GH_TOKEN=$(gh auth token)
# GITHUB_REPOSITORY=OWNER/REPO
